<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>AI Knowledge Graph – examples</title>
<style>
:root { --bg: #ffffff; --fg: #1f2328; --muted: #656d76; --panel: #f6f8fa; --border: #d0d7de; --accent: #0969da; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { :root { --bg: #0d1117; --fg: #e6edf3; --muted: #8b949e; --panel: #161b22; --border: #30363d; --accent: #388bfd; } }
body { margin: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--fg); font: 16px/1.55 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; }
main { max-width: 960px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 40px 20px 60px; }
h1 { font-size: 28px; margin: 0 0 6px; }
.lead { color: var(--muted); font-size: 17px; margin: 0 0 28px; max-width: 720px; }
.grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 14px; }
.card { display: block; text-decoration: none; color: inherit; border: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--panel); border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px 18px; }
.card:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }
.card .name { font-weight: 650; font-size: 17px; }
.card .domain { color: var(--accent); font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .05em; margin-bottom: 4px; }
.card .meta { color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; margin-top: 6px; }
.card .communities { color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; margin-top: 8px; line-height: 1.4; }
h2 { font-size: 15px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .05em; color: var(--muted); margin: 32px 0 12px; }
.how { border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); padding: 4px 16px; color: var(--muted); }
code { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 6px; font-size: 13px; }
a { color: var(--accent); }
footer { color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; margin-top: 40px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <h1>AI Knowledge Graph</h1>
  <p class="lead">Interactive knowledge graphs extracted from plain text by an LLM. Each example below was generated from a short document with
    <code>generate-graph</code>; click one to explore it: search, click a node for its relationships and source sentences, trace paths, filter by
    community or entity type.</p>
  <div class="grid">
  {% for g in graphs %}
    <a class="card" href="{{ g.href }}">
      <div class="domain">{{ g.domain }}</div>
      <div class="name">{{ g.title }}</div>
      <div class="meta">{{ g.nodes }} entities · {{ g.edges }} relationships ({{ g.inferred }} inferred) · {{ g.communities }} communities</div>
      {% if g.community_names %}<div class="communities">{{ g.community_names | join(' · ') }}</div>{% endif %}
    </a>
  {% endfor %}
  </div>
  <h2>How these were made</h2>
  <p class="how">Texts and graphs live in <code>data/samples/</code> of the repository. Extraction, entity standardization, relationship inference and
    community naming ran with <code>{{ model }}</code>; the pages were rendered with <code>generate-graph --from-json</code>. Solid lines are relationships
    stated in the text (hover for the sentence); dashed lines were inferred and are labelled with their method.</p>
  <footer><a href="https://github.com/robert-mcdermott/ai-knowledge-graph">robert-mcdermott/ai-knowledge-graph</a> on GitHub · Apache 2.0</footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
